> The MCMC distribution plots (on the right side of the MCMC dx plot layout) are essentially showing the sampling distribution of the stats under the model. Asymmetries here suggest the statistical inference may be compromised.  For small nets, you'll often see sawtooth shaped MCMC dx plots.  That is also a function of discrete, integer valued stats that only vary over a small range.  Not inherently a problem for statistical inference.
