My concern about working with the approximations is not knowing how far off the approximations are from the exact estimates, and how those approximations propagate to the other model coefficients. I know in my application, I anticipate the probability of an edge being around 0.45 but the approximation is resulting in an estimated probability of an edge at around 0.85.

If there is an alternative for implementing block-diagonal constraints, as you suggest might be possible, that would be great! Is there someone who can help to answer that question?

